        "body": "# Support intake checklist\n\nCapture only the minimum context needed for routing: symptom, feature area, severity, business impact, reproduction confidence, timeframe, and whether the issue is ongoing.\n\nUse customer-safe wording. Avoid copying identifiers, access tokens, screenshots with private data, or raw logs unless a separate approved tool explicitly requires them.\n\nDefault routing:\n\n- Product question: answer from public docs or bundled context.\n- Usage anomaly: inspect product-usage context first.\n- Integration failure: verify configuration, auth state, and recent deploy or vendor changes.\n- Data quality concern: ask for narrow examples and summarize patterns without storing private records.\n",
